meta {
  name: List Branch Lab Panel Options
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-panels/options?page=1&limit=10
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 10
  ~search: Thyroid
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Lightweight `{ id, name, price, sampleType, isFasting, isAllowDiscounts,
  isBillOnlyTest }` options for the Create-Order lab-panel picker. Returns the active
  branch's **active default-variant** lab panels only (one orderable row per variant
  group), so a selected id is directly usable as an order item's `branchLabPanelId`;
  `price` is the list price (`priceMsrp`, minor units), `sampleType` is always `null`
  (a panel has no single specimen) and `isFasting` reflects the panel's
  `isFastingRequired`.

  `isAllowDiscounts` is the inverse of the panel's `isDisableDiscount` — when
  `false` the frontend hides the panel's per-line discount input (FE-only control;
  the backend has no per-test discount gate, so an order-level discount is always
  accepted). `isBillOnlyTest` flags a billed-only panel the frontend hides from the
  workflow item list (it generates no accession samples).

  **Age Restriction:** `ageRestrictedTests` lists the panel's age-restricted
  member tests (`[]` when none), in panel order:
  `[{ branchLabTestId, testName, minAgeValue, minAgeUnit, maxAgeValue, maxAgeUnit }]`.
  Create Order blocks adding the panel when the patient's age on the order date
  is outside ANY member's range, naming that test and its range; the server
  enforces the same on `POST`/`PATCH /orders` (422 `ORDER_TEST_AGE_RESTRICTED`).

  Scoped to the JWT tenant + active branch (no `branchId` in the query). `search`
  matches panelName (case-insensitive). Omit `page` for the full array; supply `page`
  for a `{ data, total, page, limit }` envelope.
}
